To determine if there is a cycle in the graph $G$, we need to check if there is a path that starts and ends at the same node without repeating edges (or nodes, for a simple cycle).

We can use graph traversal algorithms like Breadth-First Search (BFS) or Depth-First Search (DFS) to detect cycles. During DFS, a cycle is detected if we encounter a *visited* node that is currently in the recursion stack (i.e., it is an ancestor of the current node in the DFS tree).

